                <pb facs="0429" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-24T17:00:00-04:00">September 24, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>114. Following telegram received from Legation at Monrovia:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram No. 50, September 21, 1929, noon, printed <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] From your 88, September 20, 3 p.m., the Department has assumed that
                    the Liberian Government’s request for the League to appoint a Commission member
                    is being acted upon.</p>
                <p>You may, in informally conversing with Drummond, point out that, under the terms
                    of reference issued by the Liberian Government, paragraph (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">d</hi>), Liberia has demanded an inquiry into compulsory
                    labor for public purposes as well as private. Since this affects primarily
                    Liberia, there should seem to be no objection to the League granting the request
                    of Liberia, one of its members.</p>
                <p>Replying to your 81, September 14, noon, the Department has been unable to select
                    definitely the American Commission member, but as soon as he is chosen his name
                    and biographic sketch will be communicated to you for your information. [End
                    paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
